<!DOCTYPE html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><meta name="robots" content="noindex, follow"><meta name="description" content="Begin with the changing shore, then connect the river mouth with Balasore’s literary world. Keep the reading flexible and arrange the coastal visit around local conditions."><meta name="utkal-design-system" content="0.1.0-rc.5"><meta name="theme-color" content="#91462F"><title>Balasore: places, food &amp; living culture · Project Odisha</title><link rel="canonical" href="https://projectodisha.org/destinations/balasore/"><meta name="referrer" content="no-referrer"><meta name="color-scheme" content="light"><meta property="og:type" content="website"><meta property="og:site_name" content="Project Odisha"><meta property="og:title" content="Balasore: places, food &amp; living culture · Project Odisha"><meta property="og:description" content="Begin with the changing shore, then connect the river mouth with Balasore’s literary world. Keep the reading flexible and arrange the coastal visit around local conditions."><meta property="og:url" content="https://projectodisha.org/destinations/balasore/"><meta property="og:locale" content="en_IN"><meta property="og:image" content="https://projectodisha.org/images/regions/chandipur-sunset.jpg"><meta property="og:image:alt" content="An orange sun reflected in the wet sand at Chandipur."><meta property="og:image:width" content="1280"><meta property="og:image:height" content="848"><meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image"><meta name="twitter:title" content="Balasore: places, food &amp; living culture · Project Odisha"><meta name="twitter:description" content="Begin with the changing shore, then connect the river mouth with Balasore’s literary world. Keep the reading flexible and arrange the coastal visit around local conditions."><meta name="twitter:image" content="https://projectodisha.org/images/regions/chandipur-suns